{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AUxr5ACrBHuCnhtVXJhwPH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Yurika Queensland Electric Super Highway charging price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland EV charging no longer free - carsales.com.au\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free-119547/\"},{\"title\":\"EV drivers spend average $3 and 34 minutes charging on electric superhighway\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2021/04/09/ev-drivers-spend-average-3-and-34-minutes-charging-on-electric-superhighway/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland EV charging no longer free - Servopro\",\"url\":\"https://servopro.com.au/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free/\"},{\"title\":\"Yurika / Electric Highway EV Charger Gunalda, QLD\",\"url\":\"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-gunalda-42-balkin-street\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"Yurika EV Charger Esk, QLD\",\"url\":\"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-esk-pryde-st\"},{\"title\":\"RACQ powers up Qld’s Electric Vehicle Superhighway\",\"url\":\"https://www.pv-magazine-australia.com/press-releases/racq-powers-up-qlds-electric-vehicle-superhighway/\"}]\n\nYurika's QESH charging prices have risen a lot since the network launched. The most recent figures I found are from listings about 103 days old.\n\n- **Current (Plugroo listings):**\n  - The Gunalda site lists $0.35–0.55 per kWh. That breaks down as $0.35 for the 22 kW Type 2 plugs and $0.55 for the 75 kW fast plugs.\n  - The Esk site lists $0.30–0.55 per kWh. That is $0.30 for the 22 kW Type 2 plugs and $0.55 for the 50 kW DC plugs.\n  - Plugroo is a third-party aggregator, not an official Yurika source.\n- **2020–2021:** The network charged 20 cents per kWh. The average session cost about $3.\n- **Earlier still:** The network was free at first. Reports then said a fee of 45 cents per kWh was coming. The Queensland Main Roads Minister said negotiations were underway to charge less than that. The later 20 cent rate matches that.\n- **Who sets prices:** Yurika Energy reportedly sets the prices, and Chargefox manages the network.\n\nI didn't find an official Yurika or Queensland Government price page. The Plugroo figures are the best current estimate.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a852b51-1e1e-4265-924e-2201e84b266c","uuid":"1e0ba70b-9204-43eb-8e14-f67907e234bd","timestamp":"2026-11-18T10:03:38.386Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Yurika Queensland Electric Super Highway charging price per kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019vC2QSCLodkd3xhRaGjfbQ","content":[{"title":"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com","url":"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/"},{"title":"Queensland EV charging no longer free - carsales.com.au","url":"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free-119547/"},{"title":"EV drivers spend average $3 and 34 minutes charging on electric superhighway","url":"https://thedriven.io/2021/04/09/ev-drivers-spend-average-3-and-34-minutes-charging-on-electric-superhighway/"},{"title":"Queensland EV charging no longer free - Servopro","url":"https://servopro.com.au/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free/"},{"title":"Yurika / Electric Highway EV Charger Gunalda, QLD","url":"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-gunalda-42-balkin-street"},{"title":"Queensland to ad